PASS T1 identities at the b-point: x^2 + x y + y^2 = 1, 2M = x y (x+y), f(r_b)=f(r_c)=0, kappa_b = a0, T_b/T_dS = 1/Z; at the c-point kappa_c = a0
PASS T2 A_b Lambda = 12 pi x^2 = 10.297306 (not 32 pi^2 = 315.82734): the puzzle's AREA relation does not hold at the a0-point (audit a07 S3 reproduced); S_tot/S_dS = 0.67053731
PASS T3 BH-normalised surface gravities at the b-point: kappa_b^BH = 1.8501904 H, kappa_c^BH = 1.6325638 H: both > H, so in that normalisation a0 = H/Z is NOT a horizon value (a07 S5 reproduced)
PASS T4 two static worldlines with proper acceleration a0 exist inside the b-point SdS, at r/L = 0.56952765 < r* = 0.57482825 < r/L = 0.58022778, both between the horizons (r_b = 0.52263231, r_c = 0.63039097); pure de Sitter: sin(theta0) = 1/sqrt(1+Z^2) = 0.17022584

